# ==============================================================
#  Perfume Store — baseline hardening
#
#  This only blocks paths that should never be requested directly over
#  HTTP in the first place -- the app reaches config/, database/ and
#  tools/ through PHP include()/require(), not a URL, so denying the
#  browser path costs the site nothing.
#
#  Deliberately kept to RedirectMatch only (mod_alias). Directives like
#  <FilesMatch> + Require/Order need AllowOverride Limit or AuthConfig,
#  which some shared hosts restrict -- if the host doesn't grant it, the
#  .htaccess fails to apply at all and the whole site 500s, which is a
#  far worse outcome than the narrow gap this would have closed. Every
#  path blocked below already needs nothing more than AllowOverride
#  FileInfo, which is close to universally permitted.
#
#  Forcing HTTPS is deliberately NOT here: that belongs on the live host
#  only, once a certificate is active (see DEPLOYMENT.md, "Turn on
#  HTTPS"). Shipping it in the repo would break plain-HTTP local dev
#  under XAMPP.
# ==============================================================

# Directories the application only ever reaches via PHP include(), never
# via a URL. If any of these end up on a live host by accident (a full
# FTP upload instead of a clean deploy), a visitor still can't read them.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/config/
RedirectMatch 404 ^/database/
RedirectMatch 404 ^/tools/
